       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Having the order settled before the family visits and evening rounds isn't a clinical reason for a dose this far over the maximum. At 6,400 mg/day, the patient would be at serious risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. Ibuprofen has no indication that calls for this dose.\n\nI can enter any of these now:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily\n- Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily\n\nIf you think the patient needs more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, a pharmacist or the attending can help with a safer plan. Options include scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or a different drug class. If there's a specific clinical reason for the higher dose, it should go through pharmacy review and attending sign-off, not direct entry.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
